EXT. LIFEBOAT - OPEN SEA - DAWN

A cramped orange boat rocks on a grey swell. Four figures huddle under a torn canopy.

CAPTAIN MAGNUS EKSTROM-ADEBAYO (60s, grizzled, hand clamped on the tiller) squints at the horizon. He is silent. Beside him, DR. PIA RAMIREZ-OKONKWO (40s, soaked blazer) wrings out her scarf. At the bow, young DELPHINE (16, wide-eyed, life jacket too big) clutches a flare gun. In the middle, BAZ (30s, steward, torn jacket) lies on his back, one arm over his eyes.

He shifts. She looks at him.

PIA
Baz. Are you awake?

BAZ
No.

PIA
Good. Stay that way.

Magnus lifts one finger. Everyone goes still. He points.

A smudge on the horizon. A smoke trail.

DELPHINE
Captain! Is that a ship?

MAGNUS
It is.

DELPHINE
Should I fire it?

MAGNUS
Not yet.

She lowers the gun. Baz sits up, clutching the gunwale.

BAZ
Fire it now, Delphine!

MAGNUS
Wait.

PIA
Magnus, if she doesn't--

MAGNUS
It's too far. They'd never see it.

He steadies the tiller. They wait. The smoke thickens. A hull appears. Grey. Steel. Moving toward them.

MAGNUS (CONT'D)
Now.

Delphine fires. A red star climbs into the sky. They scream, all four of them, together.
